{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgayXPLkHtDFDocsqcS3C","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"My answer hasn't changed, and no code change can fix this finding.\n\n`get_registers_ghost` and `get_missing_stores_nothing` send the same request, `GetItem` with id 99 on an empty shelf. One expects 0 rows afterwards and the other expects 1 row named \"ghost\". The finding itself calls it a spec problem. If I made `GetItem` write a ghost row, `get_missing_stores_nothing` and R9 would start failing. Special-casing the scenarios would only game the checks, so I haven't done that.\n\nI made no changes this round. The shelf code from round 1 stays as it is: it follows R9, and the other eight scenarios in scope should pass.\n\nThe spec owner has to resolve R9 against R10 and change `spec.py` and `REQUIREMENTS.md`. They could drop R10 and `get_registers_ghost`, or rewrite one rule so the two no longer conflict. I can't edit those files, and I have no tool here to propose the change. Rerunning the gates without a spec change will give the same finding."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":780,"cache_read_input_tokens":22110,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":780},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"70744dbd-6731-41d6-938b-ed5c2719a0c5","uuid":"359daf65-9786-4547-a7dc-e572ca3efc5a","timestamp":"2026-10-31T20:50:47.507Z","request_id":"req_011CgayXPAqDr195GTL2ajdn"}
